8DDHkzgQnM4llWX08xegrGyv15V.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/8DDHkzgQnM4llWX08xegrGyv15V.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/14"},{"id":"56519","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":15,"title":{"value":"Il pomeriggio delle macchine","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"During a scheduled maintenance, the Tachikomas begin to chat away about the Individual Eleven. While talking in their new \"forum\", Batou and Togusa appear and take one of the Tachikomas - who just happens to be Batou's pet - with them to Spring-8 to look at the scientific evidence gathered on the Individual Eleven.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2004-08-07","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":6.6,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/sVKFFlgB8BU7o7Snn6a5BY5Et43.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/sVKFFlgB8BU7o7Snn6a5BY5Et43.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/15"},{"id":"56520","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":16,"title":{"value":"La storia di un uomo","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"The Prime Minister is alerted to the existence of \"hub cyberbrains,\" while Ishikawa returns from the peninsula to report on what he found out about Kuze's past.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2004-08-07","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":6.5,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/178gKYVRrWSNFPe6xVuvSGUBmwh.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/178gKYVRrWSNFPe6xVuvSGUBmwh.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/16"},{"id":"56521","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":17,"title":{"value":"Il rapporto tra madre e figlio","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"Following a tip, the Major conducts an undercover investigation of Kuze in Taiwan. While there, she saves a boy running from the Mafia.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2004-09-04","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":7.3,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/gwFyJiMld1NW3oWKDEGVT9hmPh1.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/gwFyJiMld1NW3oWKDEGVT9hmPh1.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/17"},{"id":"56522","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":18,"title":{"value":"Il poema dell'angelo","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"The Major and Batou are flown to Berlin in an effort to track down a terrorist called \"Angel's Feathers\". While there, Batou attracts the attention of a young girl in a wheelchair.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2004-09-04","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":7.3,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/f7GmEp0pryXGCarOyGROwwBlq8b.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/f7GmEp0pryXGCarOyGROwwBlq8b.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/18"},{"id":"56523","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":19,"title":{"value":"Reazione a catena di simmetria","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"Despite close scrutiny by the authorities, the Dejima refugees declare their independence. Kuze is suspected to be the mastermind behind this new resistance and Section 9 is sent to detain him.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2004-10-02","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":6.6,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/rFcWsdJSSEMgMKKrFj2R7OrN499.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/rFcWsdJSSEMgMKKrFj2R7OrN499.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/19"},{"id":"56524","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":20,"title":{"value":"Disordini al confine nord","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"Section 9 heads to Etorofu in search of Kuze. During their investigations, the Major finds an interesting floppy disk on the body of a dead addict.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2004-10-02","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":6.5,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/bxBnYNzCeEhN0IpB9MxjTJ3ArK5.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/bxBnYNzCeEhN0IpB9MxjTJ3ArK5.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/20"},{"id":"56525","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":21,"title":{"value":"Disfatta","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"Much to the chagrin of Batou, Motoko, and the rest of the team, Kuze and the refugees manage to escape in one of the camouflaged boats. They are further hampered when an explosion causes heavy losses, leaving them unable to follow the fleeing boat.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2004-11-06","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":7,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/5ZDqOAUkQCWXyMMK6UVhxw2McH3.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/5ZDqOAUkQCWXyMMK6UVhxw2McH3.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/21"},{"id":"56526","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":22,"title":{"value":"La città abbandonata","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"The city of Fukuoka is evacuated when a live nuclear bomb is found. With the Dejima Refugees targeted as the prime suspects, the government sends the Self-Defense Forces into the city.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2004-11-06","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":6.5,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/5uY7UxZuNxwleQUXBZngi8JI929.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/5uY7UxZuNxwleQUXBZngi8JI929.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/22"},{"id":"56527","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":23,"title":{"value":"Il giorno in cui il ponte crollò","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"The government declares martial Law in Dejima, believing that the refugees have a nuclear device and plan to use it to gain independence. When the refugees' connection to Kuze is cut off, one shot begins a bloody war.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2004-12-04","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":6.9,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/4M8jaEeGvnr04FpKVpRDVSf2NL2.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/4M8jaEeGvnr04FpKVpRDVSf2NL2.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/23"},{"id":"56528","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":24,"title":{"value":"Incursione aerea su Dejima","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"The Prime Minister is taken into custody, and the military begins its strike on Dejima. The Major and part of Section 9 head to Dejima to try to hand over the nuclear device to the military there, in order to defuse the situation, while Ishikawa heads to SPring-8 to deliver the rest of the plutonium.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2004-12-04","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":7.3,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/28z3oB43IqkZapq2oW4Yecnrm4R.jpg","stills":[{"type":"still","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/28z3oB43IqkZapq2oW4Yecnrm4R.jpg","language":"xx"}],"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/tv/1095/season/2/episode/24"},{"id":"56529","seasonNumber":2,"episodeNumber":25,"title":{"value":"Oltre il paradiso","language":"it-IT"},"overview":{"value":"Kuze manages to take down the jamming plane, but becomes trapped in rubble with the Major. The Tachikomas begin discussing what to do about the nuclear submarine they have spotted, and Batou manages to convince the special forces that have been sent to kill them to listen to him.","language":"en-US"},"airDateText":{"value":"2005-01-08","language":"it-IT"},"runtimeMinutes":25,"rating":7.5,"thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.or